                <pb facs="0590" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg490"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 247.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Elduayen to Mr.
                            Reed.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of
                            State</hi>
                        <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Palace</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 3,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that so soon as I received your note of the 31st of March on the
                    manner in which the laws and regulations in regard to passports are applied in
                    the island of Cuba, I referred its contents to the minister of ultramar, whose
                    answer I will hasten to transmit to your excellency so soon as it arrives in my
                    power</p>
                <p>Availing, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. ELDUAYEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
